WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.101
Welcome. This video is for anyone
who sits on an interview panel.

2
00:00:08.221 --> 00:00:14.341
Two roles: the panelist,
who marks, and the interviewer,

3
00:00:14.461 --> 00:00:20.020
who as Factory HR is handed the first
interview. Ten criteria to score

4
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:23.890
and one recommendation. The recruiter
decides; your opinion is what matters.

5
00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:29.650
Who invites you? The recruiter,
or Factory HR when the first interview is

6
00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:33.329
at the factory,
picks the panel while scheduling.

7
00:00:33.449 --> 00:00:38.490
A post can have a standing committee, in
which case your name comes up every time.

8
00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.200
When an interview is scheduled
you get an email: the candidate,

9
00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:48.400
the post, which round, the Dhaka time,
a Google Meet link or the venue and room.

10
00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:53.409
And your personal marking link.
A Google Calendar invite comes too.

11
00:00:53.759 --> 00:00:58.199
If the time changes,
another email with the new and old time.

12
00:00:58.559 --> 00:01:00.079
Your link stays the same.

13
00:01:00.429 --> 00:01:03.829
The same time and place are at
the top of your marking page,

14
00:01:03.949 --> 00:01:07.509
and in the Google Calendar invite
when HR sends one; an online round

15
00:01:07.629 --> 00:01:13.149
carries its Meet link there. In person,
the room. Times are always Dhaka time.

16
00:01:13.499 --> 00:01:17.059
Click the link and the evaluation
sheet opens, no password. On the left,

17
00:01:17.659 --> 00:01:22.659
the candidate: name and mobile,
approximate age, total service, education,

18
00:01:22.779 --> 00:01:28.699
and which posts at which companies for
how long. Full CV opens the whole CV.

19
00:01:29.049 --> 00:01:34.907
On the right, ten criteria: education,
experience, training, IT knowledge,

20
00:01:35.027 --> 00:01:39.889
leadership, attitude, presentation,
discretion, and the rest.

21
00:01:40.649 --> 00:01:45.529
Four answers each; pick one,
and it shows in the heading.

22
00:01:45.879 --> 00:01:51.688
A few criteria raise questions.
Discretion: judgement, confidentiality.

23
00:01:51.808 --> 00:01:57.614
Position scarcity: how rare people
with these skills are in the market.

24
00:01:57.734 --> 00:02:02.639
Complexity of work:
how complex the post's work is.

25
00:02:03.239 --> 00:02:05.159
Give what you honestly think.

26
00:02:05.509 --> 00:02:10.029
Comments below. Then your recommendation,
required to submit:

27
00:02:10.149 --> 00:02:15.749
Select, Reject, or Talent Pool,
not for this post but worth keeping.

28
00:02:16.099 --> 00:02:21.225
The bar at the bottom shows the total,
the percentage, what is left. All done,

29
00:02:21.345 --> 00:02:27.459
Submit Evaluation. After submitting
you can read the sheet, not change it.

30
00:02:27.809 --> 00:02:33.689
The panelist from the HR Department gets
one extra section in the left panel,

31
00:02:34.049 --> 00:02:39.509
Facilities: open it for present salary,
expected salary,

32
00:02:39.629 --> 00:02:43.079
benefits and the transport pick-up point.
One record per candidate, so

33
00:02:43.199 --> 00:02:47.249
if another HR panelist changed it first,
yours is refused; reopen and write again.

34
00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:53.519
Signed in, My Interviews does the same.
To mark lists what is pending,

35
00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:58.999
Submitted what you have done, and All has
everything, cancelled rounds included.

36
00:02:59.758 --> 00:03:05.039
Open one and it is the same sheet.
Two days without marks, a reminder comes.

37
00:03:05.389 --> 00:03:11.429
A cancelled round shows as Cancelled under
All; no marks needed. Rescheduled, the new

38
00:03:11.549 --> 00:03:17.629
time with the same link. As an HR panelist
the facilities section is here too.

39
00:03:17.979 --> 00:03:22.180
And as interviewer, when the recruiter
hands you a candidate's first interview,

40
00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:27.638
Assigned Candidates: To schedule,
Scheduled, Decision due, Done.

41
00:03:27.758 --> 00:03:33.300
Schedule, Interviewed, Decide.

42
00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.779
Every screen is in Role Guide 02.

43
00:03:37.129 --> 00:03:43.062
After the interview, Decide: Yes,
and the candidate goes to the HR Head

44
00:03:43.182 --> 00:03:47.089
or straight to Final. No, with a reason,
and the regret-mail tick if you like.

45
00:03:47.929 --> 00:03:50.489
The decision is yours;
the marks are the panel's.

46
00:03:50.839 --> 00:03:56.239
Questions. Do I need a password?
No, the link is enough.

47
00:03:56.359 --> 00:04:02.239
Link not working? Tell the recruiter,
they send a New link.

48
00:04:02.359 --> 00:04:07.319
Time looks wrong?
The card says GMT+6, Dhaka time.

49
00:04:07.669 --> 00:04:09.662
Submitted the wrong marks?

50
00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:14.509
The sheet cannot be changed; tell the
recruiter, who notes it in the comments.

51
00:04:15.349 --> 00:04:19.189
Next time, glance at the percentage
on the bar before submitting.

52
00:04:19.539 --> 00:04:23.899
In short. The emailed link,
the candidate on the left,

53
00:04:24.019 --> 00:04:28.139
ten criteria on the right,
a recommendation, Submit Evaluation.

54
00:04:28.819 --> 00:04:33.299
The full guide is a PDF under Tutorials.
Thank you.

